Subject: [PATCH 71/86] Outline in Preview follows the preview scroll

In the Preview view there is no cursor to follow, so the outline now
highlights the top-most heading the preview shows, or the heading the
top line sits under when none is in view. Scrolled to the end (for
example Ctrl+End), it highlights the last heading in view, as headings
further down can never reach the top. Any preview scroll counts: wheel,
scrollbar, arrows, Page Up/Down, Home/End and Ctrl+Home/Ctrl+End. The
outline scrolls to keep the highlighted heading in view as before.

In Source and Split the highlight stays with the cursor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

